+## Qingmu reader-settings extension (pinned 1.5.0)
+
+This package copy carries a Qingmu-maintained additive patch. These APIs are not
+provided by upstream YouVersion 1.5.0 or 1.6.0. The original LICENSE is unchanged.
+
+The package root exports `getReaderSettings`, `getDefaultReaderSettings`,
+`setReaderSettings`, `subscribeReaderSettings`, and the `ReaderSettingsSnapshot`
+type. Snapshots contain only fontSize, fontFamily and lineSpacing. The original
+Reader and Settings UI continue using the same store and their original setters.
+
+`setReaderSettings` validates the entire partial object before one SDK store
+update and one SDK persistence write. Font sizes are clamped by the SDK; finite
+unsupported line spacing normalizes to the SDK default. Font families must match
+the built-in Inter/Untitled Serif stacks; the legacy Source Serif stack migrates
+through the existing SDK normalizer. Malformed numbers, unknown keys and invalid
+font strings throw TypeError without changing state. No private persistence key
+is read or written by the facade. Subscribers receive detached snapshots only
+when one of the three values changes; subscription does not emit immediately.
+
+This API does not itself provide account isolation. The host application owns
+per-member SecureStore values and its applying guard during account restoration.
+
+### Maintenance and original-file hash guard
+
+Only apply to package version 1.5.0 with these exact original SHA-256 values.
+Do not treat an upgrade or a changed file as compatible merely because a hunk
+applies. Rebase this tracked patch and rerun sdkReaderSettingsExtension.test.ts
+plus the declaration compile probe before accepting another SDK build.
